        "id": 34180,
        "name": "msbq",
        "username": "msbq",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/msbq/{size}/2824_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-07-13T17:18:36.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I LOVE THIS. A game I played just last night against The Organization ended pretty dramatically.</p>\n<p>We had Haka, Fanatic, Ra, and Legacy. Legacy had started with Inspiring Presence, so that helped us get a good +2 damage rolling every turn with Galvanize. Then, Haka picks up Savage Mana pretty quickly, and starts swallowing up all the thugs he can get to. Our environment, Atlantis, was surprisingly docile for a few turns, but eventually started messing us up a bit more. We finally get the third underboss in the trash so we can start hitting The Chairman and BOOM Haka unleashes a good 20-24 damage on The Operative, bringing her down to 10 HP. The rest of us just wail on The Chairman a bit more and that’s when our luck was golden.</p>\n<p>The next environment turn, it played Pillars of Hercules (a card that lets us double our power, play, and draw phases if we allow the Villain deck to play another card on each Hero turn). I was controlling Legacy and there it was… Take Down. For one glorious turn, the Villain deck couldn’t do a damn thing while we took two turns each (essentially). We smoked the Chairman and let the Kraken eat the Operative. MAN what a fun game that was. <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/slight_smile.png?v=9\" title=\":slight_smile:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":slight_smile:\"></p>",
        "post_number": 4,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:08:07.447Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
